---------------------------------------------------------------------------
NOTES ON SCOPE — not part of the licence, but they affect what it covers.
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. THE CODE IS ORIGINAL.
   Everything under src/, include/, ld/, host/, tools/, docs/ and
   .github/, and install.py, was written for this project. It is not derived
   from WCH's SDK, from the GBFlash firmware, or from any existing bootloader.
   No third-party source, binary or firmware image is redistributed here.

   That list covers everything a release publishes: install.py,
   bootloader.bin, requirements.txt, build_composite.py (tools/),
   backup-codeflash.py and check-bootloader-region.py (docs/), README.txt
   (tools/payload-README.txt) and this file.

   The test fixtures under host/fixtures/ are generated by host/gen_streams.py
   from a synthetic firmware image built by host/make_synthetic_fw.py, so they
   contain no vendor firmware either.

2. THE USB DESCRIPTORS ARE NOT COVERED BY THIS LICENCE.
   src/usb_desc.c contains 83 bytes transcribed from the GBFlash firmware
   image: the 18-byte device descriptor, the 39-byte configuration descriptor
   set, and the 26-byte canned CH340 vendor-reply table. They are reproduced
   rather than reinvented because the host's driver binds on exactly these
   bytes — a descriptor set differing in any field would not enumerate. They
   are not this project's to license, and the grant above does not extend to
   them.

   The device also enumerates as USB 1A86:7523, which is WCH's CH340 VID/PID,
   for the same reason.

3. THE WIRE PROTOCOL WAS REVERSE-ENGINEERED.
   It was derived from FlashGBX's open-source host implementation, from an
   independent third-party project's documentation of the same protocol, and
   cross-checked against a script published by the original hardware author.

4. ATTRIBUTION.
   FlashGBX (lesserkuma) for the host software and the protocol authority;
   simonkwng for the GBFlash hardware and original firmware; the
   gbflash_unlocker project (v1b3myC0d3) for documenting the boot-info record
   and the update protocol. None of them endorse this project or are
   responsible for it.
